---

## First Steps — Every Session

1. Read `CONTEXT.md` — current state, active phase, plan, and rules
2. Read `CLAUDE.md` — full project rules, stack, patterns, and conventions
3. Check which service/area you are assigned to (CONTEXT.md Section 11)

---

## Critical Rules (always apply)

1. **NEVER `git commit` or `git push` without explicit user confirmation**
2. Read-only git OK without asking: `status`, `diff`, `log`, `branch`, `stash`
3. Business logic ALWAYS in `services.py`, never in views
4. Use `confluent-kafka`, never `kafka-python`
5. Use `uv` for packages, never `pip install` or `requirements.txt`
6. Use `Ruff` for linting, never `flake8` or `black`
7. Use `pnpm` for frontend, never `npm` or `yarn`
8. AuditEvent is append-only (regulatory) — never UPDATE or DELETE
9. No database sharing between services
10. Emails via Celery tasks, never in Kafka consumers directly
11. Environment variables via `python-decouple`, never hardcoded
12. Tests alongside the feature, never deferred to end of phase

## Instruction Priority

```
1. CONTEXT.md       <- state + active phase rules (ALWAYS first)
2. CLAUDE.md        <- full project rules and patterns
3. This file        <- quick reference for Cline/OpenCode
4. docs/            <- detailed reference (read when needed)
5. .agents/skills/  <- generic patterns (project rules override)
```

## Architecture (quick reference)

| Service | Port | Role |
|---|---|---|
| policy-service | 8001 | Customers and policies |
| claims-service | 8002 | Claims lifecycle |
| notification-service | 8003 | Async email via Celery |
| audit-service | 8004 | Immutable event log + WebSocket |

Communication: Kafka async by default. Only sync HTTP: claims -> policy (verify).

